[size=5][b]Quest and Exploration Navigation - Fork[/b][/size]
[b]Version 1.11.4 | Experimental[/b]
Navigation for quests, map pins, collectibles and bells, with routes on the regional map and a raised guiding rope in the game world. Based on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/472]azqwq333's Quest and Exploration Navigation 0.8.5-beta[/url], independently maintained by kurosakana.

[size=4][b]Which file to install[/b][/size]
Choose one ZIP under [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/994?tab=files]Files[/url].
[list]
[*][b]1.11.4 Release:[/b] Experimental collision-based navigation across 11 worlds, for everyday play.[/*]
[*][b]1.11.4 Development:[/b] The same navigation plus 47 numbered test routes and local recording controls. Install this or Release, not both.[/*]
[*][b]1.9.4 Lite:[/b] Smaller standalone edition using the navigation data from before the full-world rebuild.[/*]
[/list]
To switch from Full to Lite, close the game and uninstall Full in UE Mod Manager before installing Lite. Keep your settings file.

[b]Development recording:[/b] Show quest items or all items in Map Tracker Plus 1.0.14, then select a numbered start/end marker. Light attack starts recording near its start and saves near its end. Heavy attack marks navigation problems; defense marks personal wrong turns. Defaults: X/left mouse, Y/F (legacy keyboard Y also works), LB/right mouse. Record only during gameplay; menus do not trigger recording. Release does not include these test markers or recording controls.

[size=4][b]Rope color (1.3.1)[/b][/size]
Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/173]PbzModConfig - Mod Settings Menu (UE4SS)[/url] and its UE4SS dependency. In the in-game Mods settings page, open Quest & Exploration Navigation → Rope color and choose Red, Blue (default), or Custom. The custom-color control appears when Custom is selected. Changes save automatically and apply within about one second. Map Tracker is not required for this setting.

[size=4][b]Changes since 1.0.1[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]1.2.1 — Controller input and grouped maps:[/b] adds D-pad polling when the game omits preview-key events, combines event/poll repeats, and fixes selection/projection of collectibles from another world within a merged chart. Each item keeps its real location and height.[/*]
[*][b]1.2.0 — Wall checks and D-pad selection:[/b] revokes expired distant-line checks before revalidation, adds triangle-collision checks after simple misses, preserves map-route corners, and marks the route beyond a known blocker as unconfirmed. D-pad focuses the nearest visible collectible in the requested direction without latching back onto native bells.[/*]
[*][b]1.1.1 — Bell identity and detours:[/b] recognizes the collector's native bell markers. Unopened bells use overland routing; blocked roadbook candidates can attempt checked local detours, including an open side passage around a closed gate. The gate remains locked.[/*]
[*][b]1.1.0 — Experimental traversal expansion:[/b] expands wall-running, wall-jump, ledge/pole and boarding recognition. Adds 487 placed interaction instances and 86 directional 3D roadbook candidates. Sailing and recognized cinematic rides retain the target and replan after ending. Candidates still require current scene and mechanism checks.[/*]
[*][b]1.0.2 — Walking and traversal connections:[/b] keeps inactive bells on overland routes, compares nearby walking before choosing a bell transfer, connects actions through checked ground corridors, and corrects down-slide entry and rappel landing handling.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Navigation features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Tracks normal quests, map pins and collectible selections. Map Tracker sync preserves the item's actual 3D position, including its floor, and follows target changes, collection and cancellation.[/*]
[*]Compares walking with activated-bell transfers. A transfer guides you to the departure bell; after you teleport manually, navigation continues toward the original item. Unloaded arrival segments remain pending.[/*]
[*]Checks floor support, character clearance, slopes, steps, known locks and recognized mechanism conditions. Blocked searches can retain a checked prefix and an unconfirmed preview while looking for a bounded detour.[/*]
[*]Shows blue calculation and loading messages with elapsed time.[/*]
[*]Retains two directed reference courses: 大廊桥 → 小张藏身处 and 乱葬岗 → 墨玑子衣冠冢, with checked same-floor joins and short item approaches.[/*]
[*]Adds 170 supplementary Chinese acquisition hints while preserving existing detailed descriptions and other languages. Collector-owned files are not replaced.[/*]
[*]The world line sits about 105 cm above the ground. No runtime trail learning or runtime downloads. Development saves local diagnostic recordings.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Route coverage[/b]
Guidance depends on the passages and mechanisms currently available. At a closed route, guidance can stop at the obstacle. The full edition is experimental.

[size=4][b]Controls[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Mouse:[/b] left-click a collectible to track it, or hover and middle-click to navigate with its actual height. Close filters before placing a map pin: middle-click blank map space; hold about 0.6 s on blank space to cancel.[/*]
[*][b]Controller:[/b] on the regional map, use D-pad to focus the nearest visible collectible in that direction, then A to confirm. Press again for the next item; holding repeats at a limited rate. Native bells/quests and hidden/collected items are skipped. Moving the stick, switching map/layer or removing the item releases focus. Empty-space A hold cancels navigation.[/*]
[*][b]Bells and actions:[/b] use the stick and normal confirmation for native bells, or middle-click their icons. Use the game controls for teleporting, climbing, grappling, ladders and lifts. Step onto an automatic slope to start sliding. Close the map for the world line; enable WorldThread. Sense30 mode first requires Sense.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements and installation[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Required:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/113]PBZModLoader 1.0.0 (#113)[/url].[/*]
[*][b]Optional settings menu:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/149]Mods Menu 0.7.2 (#149)[/url].[/*]
[*][b]For collectible sync/hints:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/187]Map Tracker Plus 1.0.14 (#187)[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/5]UE4SS for Phantom Blade Zero 1.0.3 (#5)[/url]. Tested UE4SS runtime: [b]v3.0.1-1195-g1ceefac8 Shipping[/b]; its ABI/hash check remains. Other collector versions require compatible service interfaces.[/*]
[/list]
Close the game and back up [b]ProjectPBZ/Content/Paks/~mods/PBZQuestRoute.txt[/b]. For UE Mod Manager, extract the ZIP first. Import the extracted folder containing both ProjectPBZ and platform, then select both the navigation game files and PBZQuestRouteCompat. For manual installation, disable the older navigation, move its script folder outside the game, and merge the extracted ProjectPBZ and platform folders into the game root. Keep only one navigation copy and restart the game.

The package does not include PBZModLoader, UE4SS or the collector. PBZQuestRouteCompat belongs to navigation; leave PbzMapTracker files untouched. When migrating from the old JS collector/navigation, move out the old pbz-map-tracker folder, legacy 0.7.x zzz_PBZQuestRoute_P files and PBZQuestRouteMouse. Do not run both collector generations. Legacy JS-only minimap-route, enlarged-icon and automatic-accessory options have not been ported to the UE4SS collector.

Settings: F9 → Quest & Exploration Navigation - Fork. Config: ProjectPBZ/Content/Paks/~mods/PBZQuestRoute.txt. For troubleshooting, check ProjectPBZ/PBZModLoader/loader.log, PBZQuestRoute-startup.txt in the actual Saved folder, and PBZQuestRouteCompat-status.txt in the adapter folder. The new [b]pad focus[/b] log includes input source and candidate counts.

Uninstall through the manager after closing the game. For manual removal, remove only navigation's PBZQuestRoute script/assets folders and PBZQuestRouteCompat adapter, retaining your config, collector and shared runtimes.

[size=5][b]中文说明[/b][/size]
[b]任务与探索导航 - Fork 1.11.4（实验版）[/b]
在区域地图上显示任务、标记、收集物和铃铛路线，关闭地图后显示离地约 105 厘米的导航引导线。基于 azqwq333 的原版 0.8.5-beta，由 kurosakana 独立维护。

[size=4][b]版本选择[/b][/size]
在[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/994?tab=files]文件页[/url]选装一个 ZIP。
[list]
[*][b]1.11.4 发行版：[/b]包含 11 个世界的碰撞重建导航，用于日常游玩。[/*]
[*][b]1.11.4 Development 开发版：[/b]相同导航核心，另含47段编号测试起终点和本地记录功能；与发行版选装其一。[/*]
[*][b]1.9.4 Lite：[/b]使用全图重建前的导航数据，可独立安装，下载体积更小。[/*]
[/list]
从全图版换回 Lite 时，请关闭游戏，先用 UE Mod Manager 卸载全图版，再安装 Lite。保留原配置文件。

[b]开发版录制：[/b]在Map Tracker Plus 1.0.14中显示任务物品或全部物品，选择编号路线的开始/结束点。起点附近轻攻击开始记录，终点附近轻攻击结束保存；重攻击标导航问题，防御标自己走错。默认按键为X/鼠标左键、Y/F（保留旧键盘Y）、LB/鼠标右键。仅操控角色时记录，地图与菜单不触发。发行版不含这些测试标记与采集操作。

[size=4][b]绳子颜色（1.3.1）[/b][/size]
安装[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/phantombladezero/mods/173]PbzModConfig - Mod Settings Menu (UE4SS)[/url]及其UE4SS依赖，在游戏设置的Mods页打开“任务与探索导航”→“绳子颜色”，可选红色、蓝色（默认）或自定义。选择自定义后显示颜色控件，修改后自动保存，约1秒内生效。此设置不需要安装Map Tracker。

[size=4][b]1.0.1 以来的更新[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]1.2.1：手柄输入与合并地图。[/b]补上未送达预览事件时的十字键轮询，事件和轮询共用去重与长按节流；修复合并地图中跨世界物品被误排除、投影使用错误地图 ID 的问题，保留物品真实位置和楼层。[/*]
[*][b]1.2.0：穿墙显示检查与十字键选物。[/b]远段碰撞检查过期后立即撤销旧安全终点，复查只放行已确认前段；简化碰撞未命中时补查三角面碰撞。地图保留真实拐角，已知阻挡之后显示待确认虚线。十字键可按方向选择最近可见收集物，避免焦点被原生铃铛抢回。[/*]
[*][b]1.1.1：铃铛识别与遇阻绕行。[/b]识别收集 Mod 的原生铃铛标记，未解锁铃铛使用陆路；路书候选遇阻可尝试经检查的局部绕行。门锁仍有效，但可寻找开放侧路。[/*]
[*][b]1.1.0：实验性动作扩展。[/b]扩展走壁、蹬墙跳、翻越、立柱与登船识别，接入 487 个关卡交互实例和 86 条有向三维路书候选。乘船及已识别剧情骑乘期间保留目标，结束后续算；候选仍需当前场景和机关条件检查。[/*]
[*][b]1.0.2：步行与动作接路。[/b]未激活铃铛保留陆路导航，近处物品先比较步行与铃铛中转；动作之间可用经检查的地面路网连接，并修正下滑入口与沿绳下降落点。[/*]
[/list]

[b]保留的功能[/b]
收集目标保留三维坐标，切换、收集完成和取消会同步。物品导航可比较已激活铃铛中转：先到出发铃铛，由玩家手动传送，落稳后继续原物品末段。地面、身体空间、坡度、步高、已知门锁和机关条件参与检查；受阻时可保留安全前段和未确认预览。计算或加载路网时显示蓝色提示和等待秒数。

保留大廊桥→小张藏身处、乱葬岗→墨玑子衣冠冢两条有向参考课程，以及经检查的同层接入和短物品支线。补充 170 项中文获取提示，保留收集 Mod 原有详细说明和其他语言。不替换收集文件，不采样或保存玩家通路，运行时不联网下载。

[b]导航范围[/b]
导航取决于当前通路和机关状态，通路关闭时可能只指到障碍前。全图版仍为实验版。

[b]操作[/b]
[list]
[*]鼠标：左键追踪物品，或悬停后中键导航以保留实际高度。关闭筛选后，中键点击地图空白处落旗，空白处长按约 0.6 秒取消。[/*]
[*]手柄：区域地图中按十字键吸附该方向最近的可见收集物，按 A 确认；继续按可切到下一个，长按限速切换。跳过原生铃铛、任务以及隐藏／已收集物品。移动摇杆、切图／切层或移除该物品后解除吸附。空白处长按 A 取消导航。[/*]
[*]原生铃铛仍可用摇杆和确认键选择，鼠标可中键选铃铛图标。传送、攀爬、钩索、梯子、滑索和升降装置由玩家操作，自动滑坡踏上斜坡即可触发。关闭地图查看引导线，开启 WorldThread；Sense30 模式先使用洞照。[/*]
[/list]

[b]依赖、安装与排错[/b]
必需 PBZModLoader #113（1.0.0）；可选设置菜单 Mods Menu #149（0.7.2）。需要收集联动／补充提示时，另装 Map Tracker Plus #187（1.0.14）和 UE4SS #5（1.0.3，v3.0.1-1195-g1ceefac8 Shipping）。运行时 ABI／哈希检查保留，其他收集版本仍须满足服务接口契约。

退出游戏并备份 ProjectPBZ/Content/Paks/~mods/PBZQuestRoute.txt。使用 UE Mod Manager 时，请先解压 ZIP，再导入包含 ProjectPBZ 和 platform 的解压目录，同时选择导航游戏文件与 PBZQuestRouteCompat。手动安装时，先停用旧导航、将旧脚本目录移出游戏，再把解压后的 ProjectPBZ 和 platform 合并到游戏根目录。只启用一份导航并重启游戏。

包内不含加载器、UE4SS 本体或收集 Mod。PBZQuestRouteCompat 属于导航，不要替换 PbzMapTracker 文件。迁移时移出旧 JS 收集目录、旧 0.7.x 导航文件及 PBZQuestRouteMouse，不要同时启用两代收集 Mod。旧 JS 专用的小地图路线、放大图标、自动饰品提示尚未迁移到 UE4SS 收集版。

设置菜单默认 F9，配置路径见上文。排错查看 ProjectPBZ/PBZModLoader/loader.log、实际 Saved 目录的 PBZQuestRoute-startup.txt 和桥接目录的 PBZQuestRouteCompat-status.txt；[b]pad focus[/b] 日志会记录输入来源和候选数量。卸载时退出游戏，通过管理器移除导航，或仅移除导航自己的脚本／资产和桥接目录，保留配置、收集 Mod 与共享运行时。

